---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Q1 = `bits ← [1, 0, 1, 1]
total ← 0
place ← 1
i ← LENGTH(bits)

REPEAT UNTIL(i < 1)
{
  IF(bits[i] = 1)
  {
    total ← total + place
  }
  place ← place * 2
  i ← i - 1
}

DISPLAY(total)`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Question Set 14</h1>

        <h4 class="text-sn-theme">Six questions &middot; 11 minutes &middot; cumulative</h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>What This Is</h2>

          <p>
            Six questions through Activity 2.20, weighted toward{" "}
            <b>data representation and the problems datasets have</b>.
          </p>

          <p>
            Question 1 is in exam notation. The rest are the kind of reasoning
            question the Data big idea is made of &mdash; <b>17&ndash;22% of the
            multiple-choice section</b>, and Quarter 2 is the only place this
            course teaches it.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b>Set a timer for 11 minutes.</b> Work them out on paper; do not
            run the code. Mark each answer <b>sure</b> or <b>unsure</b>. Guess
            rather than leave a blank.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="questions">
          <h2>The Questions</h2>

          <p>
            Four have exactly one correct answer, one asks you to select{" "}
            <i>all</i> that apply, and the last is about the impact of computing
            rather than about data itself.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 1</h3>

          <p>What does this display?</p>

          <Code code={Q1} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Question 1" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) 4</li>
            <li>(B) 13</li>
            <li>(C) 11</li>
            <li>(D) 1011</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 2</h3>

          <p>
            A row of 20 characters is put through a <b>lossless</b> compression
            algorithm and comes out as 24 characters. Which statement is best
            supported?
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) The original had little redundancy for this algorithm to exploit</li>
            <li>(B) The algorithm is broken and cannot be lossless</li>
            <li>(C) Information was lost during compression</li>
            <li>(D) The compression ratio is 0.83</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 3 &mdash; Select all that apply</h3>

          <p>Which of these are true?</p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) Analog data changes in discrete steps rather than smoothly</li>
            <li>(B) Analog data can be closely approximated digitally using sampling</li>
            <li>(C) Using digital data to approximate real-world analog data is an example of abstraction</li>
            <li>(D) Too low a sample rate can make two different signals produce identical samples</li>
            <li>(E) Sampling stores the original analog signal exactly</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 4</h3>

          <p>
            A counter is stored in 8 bits. It is at 255 and the program adds 1.
            What has happened?
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) The program stops with a syntax error</li>
            <li>(B) An overflow error &mdash; the value is outside the range the storage defines</li>
            <li>(C) The value is rounded to the nearest storable number</li>
            <li>(D) The storage grows to 9 bits automatically</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 5</h3>

          <p>
            A survey is collected through a form on a school website. Which action
            is most likely to <b>reduce bias</b> in the result?
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) Collect ten times as many responses through the same form</li>
            <li>(B) Remove any responses that look unusual</li>
            <li>(C) Compress the dataset so it is faster to process</li>
            <li>(D) Collect responses through an additional channel that reaches people the form misses</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 6 &mdash; Impact of Computing</h3>

          <p>
            A photo-sharing service strips location information out of photo
            metadata before publishing them. This most directly addresses a
            concern about:
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) Privacy</li>
            <li>(B) Compression ratios</li>
            <li>(C) Overflow errors</li>
            <li>(D) Scalability</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Six answers, each marked <b>sure</b> or <b>unsure</b>, plus how far
            you got when the timer went off. Worth <b>4 points</b>, graded on
            completion.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1 class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash">
          Start the Timer
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
